From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tai Xiao Xuan <xiaoxuan.tai@digipen.edu>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] game: hand mastership to a peer joining a game whose master left

Game::add_peer never touched master_actor, and Game::remove_peer only
reassigns it when the room is not empty.  Because a game outlives its
peers (the lobby keeps it for empty_game_ttl), the room can go to zero
peers with master_actor still pointing at the actor that left -- and
last_actor_id never rewinds, so the peer that joins next is handed a
different actor id and the game has no master at all.

That is fatal for Kick-Flight reconnects.  ReconnectInfo learns who the
master is from the MasterClientId game property carried in the join
response, so a client that rejoins an emptied battle room is told it is
not the master; UpdateReconnectWait then takes its non-master branch,
bails on ReconnectInfo.IsSerializeRead == false every frame (waiting for
a ReconnectSharedInfo RPC from a master that no longer exists) and ends
in BeginReconnectFailed once the reconnect budget runs out.  Assign
mastership to the joiner whenever no live peer holds it.
---
 src/game.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/game.cpp b/src/game.cpp
index 0a4c16f..496e988 100644
--- a/src/game.cpp
+++ b/src/game.cpp
@@ -169,6 +169,16 @@ GamePeer *Game::add_peer(GamePeer&& game_peer) {
     // Add peer to list
     auto& fres = peers.emplace_back(game_peer);

+    // master_actor is only ever reassigned in remove_peer(), and only while somebody else is still
+    // in the room.  A game outlives its peers (it stays in the lobby for empty_game_ttl), so a peer
+    // joining a game that emptied keeps finding master_actor pointing at the actor that left.  It is
+    // told as much through the MasterClientId game property, and its client-side reconnect state
+    // machine then waits forever for a master that no longer exists -- the reconnecting player is
+    // dropped instead of resumed.  Hand mastership to the joiner whenever the current holder is not
+    // around anymore; same rule remove_peer() applies when the room is not empty.
+    if (!find_peer(master_actor))
+        master_actor = fres.actor_id;
+
     // Remove user from expected users
     expected_users.erase(peer->persistent->user_id);

